1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,770
Most of the day, this screen is off.

2
00:00:02,820 --> 00:00:07,810
Turn it on, and it sells you something, or hands you a
feed with no end.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:12,892
Today makes it something else.

4
00:00:12,942 --> 00:00:19,622
It stays on, in the room she already lives in, and it
holds the shape of her day. Built for the glance —

5
00:00:19,672 --> 00:00:22,470
coming in the door, cooking, on the way out.

6
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:36,590
It opens by bringing up the thing she's been letting
slide. Her own dentist. Not to chase her — to say it hasn't forgotten.

7
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:46,310
Then she tells it about her day, however it comes out. One
line. Nobody has time for a form.

8
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:49,553
She never touches the television.

9
00:00:49,603 --> 00:00:55,290
Five seconds later it catches up on its own, already
knowing the baby was up in the night.

10
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:00,289
Remembering is the easy half.

11
00:01:00,339 --> 00:01:08,150
The hard half is the things that never move, because every
time she thinks of one, she has to work out where to start again.

12
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:17,050
So it doesn't hand the whole thing back. It puts one move
on today.

13
00:01:19,800 --> 00:01:28,893
Underneath it's broken down, and every step carries the
moment it fits into. But she only ever gets one.

14
00:01:28,943 --> 00:01:31,530
Tomorrow's arrives on its own.

15
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:38,924
Ask it something it doesn't know and it looks it up.

16
00:01:38,974 --> 00:01:41,305
But it doesn't hand back a search page.

17
00:01:41,355 --> 00:01:43,930
It reads what it found against this family.

18
00:01:49,500 --> 00:01:52,615
An eight-month-old who isn't walking yet.

19
00:01:52,665 --> 00:01:56,242
And one line that isn't about the baby at all —

20
00:01:56,292 --> 00:01:59,870
which of the three is the most restful for her.

21
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:05,836
It writes what it found into the thing itself —

22
00:02:05,886 --> 00:02:08,430
where, what it suits, what it costs.

23
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:14,030
No shopping. No feed. No progress bars.

24
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:18,339
It won't choose for her.

25
00:02:18,389 --> 00:02:26,050
It tells her what each one costs her, and hands the choice
back. It isn't a today. It's her today.

26
00:02:31,500 --> 00:02:31,957
Today.

27
00:02:32,007 --> 00:02:35,170
A small tiger who keeps today for you.
